title: In-cluster endpoint is built without brackets for an IPv6 KUBERNETES_SERVICE_HOST
updated: 2026-10-18T06:32:31Z
---

`_in_cluster_api` (lib/Kubernetes/REST/Kubeconfig.pm:527-532) builds `"https://$host:$port"` from `KUBERNETES_SERVICE_HOST` / `KUBERNETES_SERVICE_PORT`. In an IPv6-only or IPv6-primary dual-stack cluster the kubelet sets the host to an address literal such as `fd00:10:96::1`, which gives `https://fd00:10:96::1:443` - not a valid URL; LWP and HTTP::Tiny cannot split host and port. client-go uses `net.JoinHostPort` for the same two variables. Net::Async::Kubernetes and Kubernetes::Comb reach the in-cluster case through this method.

Done when: a host containing ':' is wrapped in '[...]', with a test in t/14_kubeconfig.t (or next to the in-cluster tests) for an IPv4, an IPv6 and a DNS-name host.

